1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Develop a Python-based GPU-Accelerated CRISPR Alignment Engine that processes DNA sequences, performs sequence alignment, identifies matching regions, evaluates alignment accuracy, and compares CPU and GPU execution performance.

The project should demonstrate:

- Python development.
- DNA sequence processing.
- CRISPR guide sequence handling.
- Sequence alignment algorithms.
- GPU acceleration.
- Performance optimization.
- Testing and debugging.
- GitHub version control.
- Project documentation.

2. TECHNOLOGY STACK

Programming Language:

- Python 3.x

Libraries:

- NumPy
- Biopython
- CuPy or Numba (GPU acceleration, depending on hardware)
- Matplotlib
- Pandas
- Pytest

Development Tools:

- Visual Studio Code
- Git
- GitHub
- Jupyter Notebook (optional)

GPU:

- NVIDIA CUDA-compatible GPU, if available.
- CPU implementation as a baseline.
- GPU implementation only when compatible hardware and drivers are available.

